# Phase 14 plan 06 (OPS-01, T-14-28). The build context is a second copy of
# this tree that scripts/check-root-hygiene.mjs's env-file blacklist does NOT
# police -- everything excluded here is excluded from every image's build
# context, never just from the final layer, so nothing on this list can leak
# into an image even via an intermediate layer that a later layer "deletes".

# Dependency trees -- reinstalled fresh inside the image via `npm ci`.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Compiled output -- rebuilt fresh inside the image; a stale host-machine
# dist/ copied into the build context could silently shadow what the image
# actually compiles.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build

# VCS metadata -- irrelevant to the build, and .git can be large.
.git
.gitignore

# GSD planning artifacts and generated docs -- not part of the runtime, and
# .planning/ is this repo's own gitignored working directory.
.planning
docs
AGENTS.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
CONVENTIONS.md
README.md
SPECIFICATION.md

# Test output, coverage, and Playwright artifacts.
coverage
coverage-baseline.json
**/coverage
playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results

# CI-only configuration -- never needed inside an image.
.github

# Env files -- the single most important entry on this list (T-14-28). Every
# variant this repo's own scripts/check-root-hygiene.mjs blacklists, plus the
# checked-in example (harmless alone, but no reason to ship it either).
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Editor/OS noise.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Docker itself -- never copy Dockerfiles/compose/certs into a build context;
# a build context including its own Dockerfile is a common accidental-secret
# vector once someone adds a build ARG default here.
docker/certs
docker-compose.yml
